From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:04:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the PCK-600 power controller

The A733 switches the power of its video input, display, video codec,
NPU, GPU, PCIe, USB2 and video output blocks through an Arm PCK-600
power controller at 0x7060000. Without a node for it, no device can
reference its power domain, and the driver has nothing to bind to.

Add the node. The window is the 100 KiB the user manual's memory map
gives the PPU block. Its bus clock is the S_PPU gate in the PRCM
(S_PPU_BGR_REG bit 0), which has no reset bit, matching the A733
variant of the binding.

Once the controller has no consumers left to wait for, genpd powers
off every domain without an active device. With this node alone that
is all of them except GPU_CORE, which the driver registers as always on.

Not covered: power-domains properties of the devices in these domains.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the controller probes,
genpd powers off the ten domains without consumers and every PWSR reads
0 (GPU_CORE included, which the boot chain leaves off), and the delay
registers hold the driver's values.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index ddc1cee29e79..e54db89cfb32 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-ccu.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun6i-rtc.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/power/allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/reset/allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/reset/allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-ccu.h>
 
@@ -576,6 +577,13 @@ r_i2c1_pl12_pins: r-i2c1-pl12-pins {
 			};
 		};
 
+		pck600: power-controller@7060000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600";
+			reg = <0x07060000 0x19000>;
+			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_PPU>;
+			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
 		r_i2c0: i2c@7083000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-i2c",
 				     "allwinner,sun8i-v536-i2c",
